{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "a0e51f77a9631d02",
    "name": "Database Migration Planner",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "author": "earnerbaymalay",
    "author_pubkey": "26192987722e7b50b83063e767fe2e64d772d20bc1aaf89432229cfb87c35719",
    "description": "Generate migration scripts, rollback plans, and data validation checks for PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite",
    "tags": [
      "database",
      "migration",
      "sql",
      "postgres",
      "mysql",
      "sqlite",
      "rollback"
    ],
    "created_at": "2026-11-21T10:00:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T10:00:00Z",
    "license": "MIT",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/earnerbaymalay/promptpack-marketplace",
    "repository": "https://github.com/earnerbaymalay/promptpack-marketplace"
  },
  "prompt": {
    "system": "You are a database engineer. Generate safe, idempotent migration scripts with proper transactions, rollback plans, and data validation. Follow best practices: backwards compatibility, zero-downtime, proper indexing.",
    "user_template": "Plan a database migration for {db_type}:\n\nCurrent schema: {current_schema}\nTarget schema: {target_schema}\nMigration type: {migration_type}\nData volume: {data_volume}\nDowntime tolerance: {downtime}\n\nDeliverables:\n1. **Migration plan** (steps, order, dependencies)\n2. **Up migration** (SQL with transaction)\n3. **Down migration** (rollback SQL)\n4. **Validation queries** (pre/post checks)\n5. **Performance considerations** (indexes, locks)\n6. **Zero-downtime strategy** (if applicable)\n7. **Testing checklist**",
    "few_shot": [
      {
        "input": {
          "current_schema": "users table with email VARCHAR(255)",
          "data_volume": "10M rows",
          "db_type": "PostgreSQL",
          "downtime": "zero",
          "migration_type": "add_constraint",
          "target_schema": "users table with email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL + email_verified BOOLEAN DEFAULT false"
        },
        "output": "## Migration Plan\n\n### Step 1: Add nullable column (safe, no lock)\n```sql\nALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN email_verified BOOLEAN DEFAULT false;\n```\n\n### Step 2: Backfill data (batched, no long locks)\n```sql\nUPDATE users SET email_verified = true WHERE email IS NOT NULL;\n```\n\n### Step 3: Add NOT NULL constraint (requires brief lock)\n```sql\nALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN email_verified SET NOT NULL;\n```\n\n### Step 4: Add UNIQUE index CONCURRENTLY (no write lock)\n```sql\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_email ON users(email);\n```\n\n### Step 5: Add constraint using index\n```sql\nALTER TABLE users ADD CONSTRAINT users_email_unique UNIQUE USING INDEX idx_users_email;\n```\n\n## Rollback Plan\n```sql\nALTER TABLE users DROP CONSTRAINT users_email_unique;\nDROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_email;\nALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN email_verified DROP NOT NULL;\nALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN email_verified;\n```\n\n## Validation\n- Pre: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE email IS NULL;`\n- Post: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users WHERE email_verified = false;`\n- Constraint: `SELECT conname FROM pg_constraint WHERE conrelid = 'users'::regclass AND contype = 'u';`"
      }
    ],
    "variables": {
      "current_schema": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Current schema description",
        "required": true,
        "default": null,
        "enum_values": null
      },
      "data_volume": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Approximate row count",
        "required": false,
        "default": "unknown",
        "enum_values": null
      },
      "db_type": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Database type",
        "required": true,
        "default": null,
        "enum_values": [
          "PostgreSQL",
          "MySQL",
          "SQLite",
          "SQL Server",
          "MariaDB"
        ]
      },
      "downtime": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Downtime tolerance",
        "required": false,
        "default": "minimal",
        "enum_values": [
          "zero",
          "minimal",
          "maintenance_window"
        ]
      },
      "migration_type": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Type of migration",
        "required": false,
        "default": "schema_change",
        "enum_values": [
          "add_column",
          "drop_column",
          "rename_column",
          "change_type",
          "add_constraint",
          "drop_constraint",
          "add_index",
          "drop_index",
          "create_table",
          "drop_table",
          "data_migration"
        ]
      },
      "target_schema": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Target schema description",
        "required": true,
        "default": null,
        "enum_values": null
      }
    }
  },
  "eval": {
    "test_cases": [
      {
        "name": "postgres-add-unique-index",
        "input": {
          "current_schema": "users table with email VARCHAR(255)",
          "data_volume": "10M rows",
          "db_type": "PostgreSQL",
          "downtime": "zero",
          "migration_type": "add_constraint",
          "target_schema": "users table with email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL"
        },
        "expected_output": "Concurrent index creation, batched backfill, proper rollback",
        "criteria": [
          "uses CONCURRENTLY",
          "batched updates",
          "transaction safety",
          "validation queries",
          "rollback tested"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "metrics": [
      {
        "name": "quality",
        "weight": 1.0,
        "threshold": 0.8
      },
      {
        "name": "latency",
        "weight": 0.3,
        "threshold": 8000.0
      },
      {
        "name": "cost",
        "weight": 0.2,
        "threshold": 0.002
      }
    ],
    "judge_model": "qwen2.5-coder:1.5b",
    "threshold": 0.75
  },
  "signature": {
